  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 121 AM MST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nConditions remain quiet this morning, as high clouds have moved over \nareas west of the Divide in the last several hours since Tuesday \nevening. These are due to a closed low pressure system that is \nmoving over northern UT currently and will continue to track \neastward through the day today. Isolated light rain showers will be \npossible along and south of a Afton-to-Rock Springs line this \nafternoon as this system moves over CO. Little to no impacts will \noccur due to a lack of instability and any possible measurable \nprecipitation is likely to occur closer to the low center over \nsouthern Sweetwater County. Otherwise, conditions will be benign \nacross the CWA with seasonal temperatures and light winds. These \nconditions will be in place again Thursday as an area of high \npressure shifts over eastern MT/the western Dakotas. Above \nnormal temperatures will return for much of Johnson County as a \nresult.\n\nA trough will move over the region on Friday, shifting the area of \nhigh pressure over the Dakotas and Upper Midwest. No significant \nimpacts are expected with the passage of the trough, however the GFS \nis progging a low chance for rain over northern portions. A broad \nridge will then build over much of the Intermountain West and extend \nover the Northern Rockies by Saturday keeping conditions dry. \nTemperatures then trend above normal across the CWA by Sunday and \nremain in place through the middle of next week as the ridge folds \nover. Conditions also look to stay dry through this period, with a \nweak trough possibly moving over the area on Tuesday.",
